    },
    "message": "Move the plain decisions' effect of a proposal to Rust\n\n_apply_proposal splits into _apply_effect, what the decision does to the world, and the record.\nThe kernel takes wait, rest, sleep without a temporary room, and the three social actions: a social\naction's event is a row, with the state it captures. The other actions go to the Python step.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
